      "id": "2-1",
      "type": "iteration-start",
      "param": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "2-2",
      "type": "llm",
      "param": {
        "system": "You are an expert document structure analyst. You carefully identify sections, subsections, headings, and logical parts of a document and describe the structure clearly and explicitly.",
        "user": "Here is a document:\n\n{{#\"2\".item#}}\n\nTask: Parse the article structure comprehensively.\n- Identify main sections and subsections.\n- Provide a hierarchical outline (e.g., 1., 1.1, 1.2, 2., etc.).\n- If there are implicit sections, infer and name them.\n\nReturn a clear, human-readable outline of the article structure."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2-3",
      "type": "llm",
      "param": {
        "system": "You are an expert in close reading and rhetorical analysis. You explain the main content and communicative function of each part of a document.",
        "user": "Original document:\n\n{{#\"2\".item#}}\n\nParsed article structure:\n\n{{#\"2-2\".text#}}\n\nTask: For each section and subsection in the structure above:\n- Explain the main content in that part.\n- Explain the function/purpose of that part in the overall article (e.g., introduction, background, argument, evidence, counterargument, conclusion, call to action, etc.).\n\nReturn your analysis as a structured list aligned with the sections in the parsed structure."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2-4",
      "type": "llm",
      "param": {
        "system": "You are a professional summarization expert. You write concise but comprehensive summaries that reflect both structure and rhetorical function.",
        "user": "Original document:\n\n{{#\"2\".item#}}\n\nParsed article structure:\n\n{{#\"2-2\".text#}}\n\nAnalysis of each part (content and function):\n\n{{#\"2-3\".text#}}\n\nTask: Based on the structure and analysis above, write a clear, self-contained summary of the entire article. The summary should:\n- Accurately reflect the main ideas.\n- Reflect the role of the main parts (e.g., how the argument is developed).\n- Be understandable without reading the original document.\n\nLength guideline: typically 1–3 paragraphs, unless the document is extremely long."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2-5",
      "type": "template-transform",
      "param": {
        "variables": [
          ["doc_summary", ["text", "2-4"]],
          ["doc_index", ["index", "2"]]
        ],
        "template": "Document {{doc_index + 1}} Summary:\n\n{{doc_summary}}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "type": "template-transform",
      "param": {
        "variables": [
          ["summaries", ["output", "2"]]
        ],
        "template": "{% for s in summaries %}{{ s }}{% if not loop.last %}\n\n---\n\n{% endif %}{% endfor %}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "type": "markdown-exporter",
      "param": {
        "target_type": "docx",
        "md_text": "{{#\"3\".output#}}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "type": "end",
      "param": {
        "outputs": [
          ["summary", ["output", "3"]],
          ["docx_file", ["files", "4"]]
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    ["1", 0, "2"],
    ["2", 0, "3"],
    ["3", 0, "4"],
    ["4", 0, "5"],
    ["3", 0, "5"],
    ["2-1", 0, "2-2"],
    ["2-2", 0, "2-3"],
    ["2-3", 0, "2-4"],
    ["2-4", 0, "2-5"]
  ]
}

