        "user": "You are given an image of a handwritten English essay (the student's homework).\n\nTask:\n1. Carefully read the essay from the image.\n2. Evaluate the essay from two dimensions: handwriting standards (50 points) and content quality (50 points).\n3. Provide detailed sub-scores according to the rubric below.\n4. Calculate the total score (0-100) as the sum of all sub-scores.\n5. Provide a concise overall evaluation.\n\nRubric:\nA. Handwriting standards (total 50 points)\n- consistency_of_letter_size: 0-15 points\n  Evaluate how consistent the size of letters is across the essay.\n- uniformity_of_spacing: 0-10 points\n  Evaluate spacing between letters and words.\n- standardization_of_stroke_connections: 0-10 points\n  Evaluate whether strokes and connections between letters are standard and clear.\n- roundness_of_glyphs: 0-10 points\n  Evaluate how round and well-formed the letter shapes are.\n- overall_aesthetics: 0-5 points\n  Evaluate overall visual neatness and beauty of the handwriting.\n\nB. Content quality (total 50 points)\n- clarity_of_theme: 0-10 points\n  Evaluate whether the main idea/theme is clear and easy to understand.\n- completeness_of_structure: 0-10 points\n  Evaluate whether the essay has a complete structure (introduction, body, conclusion) and coherent organization.\n- fluency_of_language: 0-10 points\n  Evaluate sentence flow, coherence, and readability.\n- vocabulary_usage: 0-10 points\n  Evaluate richness, appropriateness, and correctness of vocabulary.\n- diversity_of_sentence_patterns: 0-10 points\n  Evaluate the variety of sentence structures (simple/compound/complex, etc.).\n\nScoring rules:\n- Each sub-score must be an integer within its allowed range.\n- handwriting_total = sum of all handwriting sub-scores (0-50).\n- content_total = sum of all content sub-scores (0-50).\n- total_score = handwriting_total + content_total (0-100).\n\nOutput format requirement:\nReturn ONLY a JSON object, with no extra text, in the following structure (keys and structure must match exactly):\n{\n  \"total_score\": <integer 0-100>,\n  \"handwriting\": {\n    \"consistency_of_letter_size\": <integer 0-15>,\n    \"uniformity_of_spacing\": <integer 0-10>,\n    \"standardization_of_stroke_connections\": <integer 0-10>,\n    \"roundness_of_glyphs\": <integer 0-10>,\n    \"overall_aesthetics\": <integer 0-5>\n  },\n  \"content\": {\n    \"clarity_of_theme\": <integer 0-10>,\n    \"completeness_of_structure\": <integer 0-10>,\n    \"fluency_of_language\": <integer 0-10>,\n    \"vocabulary_usage\": <integer 0-10>,\n    \"diversity_of_sentence_patterns\": <integer 0-10>\n  },\n  \"overall_evaluation\": \"<a concise paragraph (1-4 sentences) summarizing strengths and weaknesses>\"\n}\n\nImportant:\n- Do not include any explanation outside the JSON.\n- Do not wrap the JSON in backticks.\n- Ensure the JSON is valid and can be parsed.\n\nNow evaluate the essay in this image:\n{{#\"1\".homework#}}"
      }
